Input: {"question": "When is the feast day of Saint Marcellus?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "Marcellus of Capua Marcellus of Capua was a third- or fourth-century martyr who was inserted in the General Roman Calendar in the 13th century."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 144, "end": 228, "text": "He is recognized as a saint by the Catholic Church, with 7 October as his feast day."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 229, "end": 508, "text": "Untrustworthy legends associated him with a Saint Apuleius, which led to them being mentioned together in some editions of the Roman Martyrology, but the name of Apuleius has been removed from that official list of saints of the Catholic Church, as without historical foundation."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d00", "start": 509, "end": 603, "text": "In the Tridentine Calendar, Marcellus was commemorated with Apuleius and two other saints on 7"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 0, "end": 201, "text": "CatholicSaints.Info » Blog Archive » Saint Marcellus of Capua CatholicSaints.Info notes about your extended family in heaven Saint Marcellus of Capua Memorial 7 October Profile Student of Simon Magus ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 202, "end": 363, "text": "Converted to Christianity by Saint Peter the Apostle ; an old tradition says that he was one of the people who interred the body of Saint Peter on Vatican Hill ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 364, "end": 372, "text": "Martyr ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d01", "start": 373, "end": 592, "text": "Died in Capua , Italy buried outside the walls of Rome , Italy Canonized Pre-Congregation Additional Information Lives of the Saints , by Father Alban Butler books Our Sunday Visitor ’ s Encyclopedia of Saints sitios en"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d02", "start": 0, "end": 650, "text": "links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia ( Redirected from Marcellus of Capua ) Saint Marcellus Born third or fourth century Capua , Campania Died third or fourth century Capua , Campania Venerated in Catholic Church Eastern orthodox church Canonized pre-congregation Feast 7 October Marcellus"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (Redirected from Marcellus of Capua)"}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 75, "end": 90, "text": "Saint Marcellus"}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 91, "end": 137, "text": "Born: Third or fourth century, Capua, Campania"}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 138, "end": 184, "text": "Died: Third or fourth century, Capua, Campania"}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 185, "end": 239, "text": "Venerated in: Catholic Church, Eastern Orthodox Church"}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 240, "end": 267, "text": "Canonized: Pre-congregation"}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 268, "end": 285, "text": "Feast: 15 January"}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d03", "start": 286, "end": 295, "text": "Marcellus"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 0, "end": 41, "text": "On 7 October, the feast day of Pope Mark."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 42, "end": 102, "text": "The Sacramentarium of Pope Gelasius assigned a mass to them."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 103, "end": 240, "text": "[4] In 1716, this day became the feast of Our Lady of the Rosary, and the commemoration of Marcellus and Apuleius was moved to 8 October."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 241, "end": 413, "text": "In 1969, Marcellus was reassigned to 15 December, while Apuleius was expunged from the official list of saints of the Catholic Church, [5] as without historical foundation."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d04", "start": 414, "end": 490, "text": "[3] Although the veneration of the two saints is very old, their existing..."}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 0, "end": 87, "text": "Marcellus of Tangier Saint Marcellus of Tangier or Saint Marcellus the Centurion () (c."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 88, "end": 200, "text": "mid 3rd century – 298 AD) is venerated as a Martyr Saint by the Catholic Church and the Eastern Orthodox Church."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 201, "end": 243, "text": "His feast day is celebrated on October 30."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 244, "end": 473, "text": "Marcellus was said to have been a centurion stationed at Tingis (modern-day Tangiers) who refused to participate in the general birthday celebrations of the Emperor Maximian, which would have entailed sacrifice to the Roman gods."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 474, "end": 557, "text": "Throwing off his military belt, weapons, and vine staff (the insignia of his rank)."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d05", "start": 558, "end": 605, "text": "Marcellus was soon brought before a judge named"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "apostate who had denied the Faith even before the outbreak of persecution."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 75, "end": 140, "text": "The tyrannical Maxentius had the pope seized and sent into exile."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 141, "end": 377, "text": "This took place at the end of 308 or the beginning of 309 according to the passages cited above from the \"Catalogus Liberianus\", which gives the length of the pontificate as no more than one year, six (or seven) months, and twenty days."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 378, "end": 450, "text": "Marcellus died shortly after leaving Rome, and was venerated as a saint."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 451, "end": 581, "text": "His feast day was 16 January, according to the \"Depositio episcoporum\" of the Chronography of 354 and every other Roman authority."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d06", "start": 582, "end": 595, "text": "Nevertheless,"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d07", "start": 0, "end": 43, "text": "`` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?"}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0469-7828c2772b82:d07", "start": 44, "end": 752, "text": "title=Pope_Marcellinus & oldi